9. Canteens.—(1) The appropriate Government may make rules requiring that in any specified establishment or class of establishments employing more than the prescribed number of motor transport workers, one or more canteens shall be provided and maintained by the employer for the use of motor transport workers.
(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing power, such rules may provide for—
(a) the date by which canteen facilities shall be provided;
(b) the standards in respect of construction, accommodation, furniture and other equipment of the canteen;
(c) the foodstuffs to be served therein and the charges therefor;
(d) the constitution of a managing committee for the canteen and representation of the motor transport workers in the management of the canteen.

